{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1637","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Yet Another Minimization Problem"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given two arrays $$$a$$$ and $$$b$$$, both of length $$$n$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You can perform the following operation any number of times (possibly zero): select an index $$$i$$$ ($$$1 \\leq i \\leq n$$$) and swap $$$a_i$$$ and $$$b_i$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's define the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cost"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of the array $$$a$$$ as $$$\\sum_{i=1}^{n} \\sum_{j=i + 1}^{n} (a_i + a_j)^2$$$. Similarly, the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cost"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of the array $$$b$$$ is $$$\\sum_{i=1}^{n} \\sum_{j=i + 1}^{n} (b_i + b_j)^2$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Your task is to minimize the total "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cost"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of two arrays."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test case consists of several test cases. The first line contains a single integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\leq t \\leq 40$$$) — the number of test cases. The following is a description of the input data sets."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains an integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1 \\leq n \\leq 100$$$) — the length of both arrays."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line of each test case contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n$$$ ($$$1 \\leq a_i \\leq 100$$$) — elements of the first array."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The third line of each test case contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$b_1, b_2, \\ldots, b_n$$$ ($$$1 \\leq b_i \\leq 100$$$) — elements of the second array."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$100$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, print the minimum possible total cost."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n1\n3\n6\n4\n3 6 6 6\n2 7 4 1\n4\n6 7 2 4\n2 5 3 5\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n0\n987\n914\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case, in one of the optimal answers after all operations $$$a = [2, 6, 4, 6]$$$, $$$b = [3, 7, 6, 1]$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The cost of the array $$$a$$$ equals to $$$(2 + 6)^2 + (2 + 4)^2 + (2 + 6)^2 + (6 + 4)^2 + (6 + 6)^2 + (4 + 6)^2 = 508$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The cost of the array $$$b$$$ equals to $$$(3 + 7)^2 + (3 + 6)^2 + (3 + 1)^2 + (7 + 6)^2 + (7 + 1)^2 + (6 + 1)^2 = 479$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The total cost of two arrays equals to $$$508 + 479 = 987$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"D","problemCode":"1637D","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1637/problem/D"}